From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:13:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] spurs: _cellSpursLFQueueInitialize and
 _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody without libsre

A title whose PPU feeds an SPU task through a SPURS lock-free queue (an
ANY2ANY CellSpursLFQueue: Killzone HD's Edge zlib requests, from its level
streaming and its music loader) needs the queue's PPU side. The runtime had an
initializer that wrote a guessed line and no push, so Killzone HD ran the
firmware's own libsre for both, lifted from the player's PS3 system software
4.93. The new libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c does what libsre does, as context
handlers on the caller's reservation (the lifter's lwarx/ldarx and
stwcx./stdcx. primitives, so other PPU threads and SPU GETLLAR/PUTLLC see the
same atomicity as with the lifted libsre):

- Initialize (libsre 0x02017134, 0x0200209C, 0x02001F6C): its argument checks,
  the +0x2C init state, the SDK-version checks and the bytes it writes.
- PushBody (libsre 0x020171B8): the ANY2ANY reserve (0x020030B8) and commit
  (0x020035C8) arithmetic, the out-of-order commit mask, the wake-ups of the
  pop and push waiters from their id rings, one per element made visible, and
  the dispatch (0x0200439C) through cellSpursSendSignal, with a SPURS-owned
  queue's (spurs | 1, wid << 8 | task) resolved by patch 1001's table.

Written from a reading of the firmware 4.93 libsre PPU code (Ghidra and the
disassembly); RPCS3 was not used. After Project Pyrrhus patch 6003 (MIT),
which did the same for a direction-2 queue: the waiter rings, the commit mask
and the approach.

One difference on purpose: a blocking push into a full queue (or one with
push waiters ahead) does not register a PPU waiter and sleep on the queue's
lv2 event queue, which only cellSpursLFQueueAttachLv2EventQueue creates and
which this runtime answers without creating; it retries until there is room.
A direction-2 push is not written (logged; libsre's answer for directions 0
and 1, CELL_SYNC_ERROR_PERM, is). The old initializer in cellSpurs.c stays
for the generated NID table; the context handlers take the NIDs first.
PS3_LFQ_TRACE=1 (default off) logs every push.

Checked against libsre itself: 42,000 random lines and arguments run through
both (Killzone HD's port, a local harness with the player's libsre) gave the
same result, the same 128-byte line, the same element buffer and the same
wake-ups in every case. tools/tests/test_lfqueue.sh replays 103 of those
cases, the game's own init, the blocking push and the signal routing.
Upstream candidate.
---
 libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c | 386 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 runtime/ppu/ppu_sysprx.cpp    |   3 +
 2 files changed, 389 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c

diff --git a/libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c b/libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..727ac12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellSpursLFQueue.c
@@ -0,0 +1,386 @@
+/* cellSpursLFQueue.c -- the PPU side of the SPURS lock-free queue (CellSpursLFQueue: one 128-byte line in guest
+ * memory whose consumer, and possibly other producers, are SPU tasks), without the firmware's libsre.
+ *
+ * _cellSpursLFQueueInitialize and _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody, for an ANY2ANY queue (direction 3). Written for this
+ * runtime from a reading of the firmware 4.93 libsre PPU code (addresses at its load base 0x02000000 below): the
+ * checks, the bytes the initializer writes, the reserve and commit arithmetic and the order of the wake-ups are its
+ * own, so the line holds the same values after each call as it does with libsre. RPCS3 was not used. After Project
+ * Pyrrhus patch 6003 (MIT), which did the same for a direction-2 queue (Killzone 2) and showed the approach: the
+ * signal ring of waiter ids, the out-of-order commit mask and the line lock.
+ *
+ * Line layout (big-endian), as the ANY2ANY code uses it:
+ *   +0x00 u64 Q: u16 pops committed | u16 pop commit mask | u16 pop-waiter pack | u16 pops reserved
+ *   +0x08 u64 P: u16 pushes committed | u16 push commit mask | u16 push-waiter pack | u16 pushes reserved
+ *   +0x10 u32 size  +0x14 u32 depth  +0x18 u64 buffer (bit 0 set for ANY2ANY)  +0x20 u8,u8 0xFF 0xFF (ANY2ANY)
+ *   +0x24 u32 direction  +0x28 u32 event port of a PPU pop waiter  +0x2C u32 init state (1 running, 2 done)
+ *   +0x30 u16 port high  +0x32 u16[15] ids of the pop waiters  +0x50 u16 port low  +0x52 u16[15] ids of the push
+ *   waiters  +0x70 u64 eaSignal (the owner: a taskset, or a SPURS instance | 1)  +0x7C u32 event queue
+ * Indices run modulo 2 * depth; the element slot is the index modulo depth. A waiter pack holds three 5-bit counters
+ * modulo 30: bits 10-14 waiters woken, 5-9 wake-ups taken, 0-4 waiters registered; a waiter's id sits in the array
+ * at its counter modulo 15. Ids are (workload id << 8) | task id; 0xFFFF is a waiting PPU thread.
+ *
+ * What differs from libsre, on purpose: a blocking push into a queue that is full (or that has push waiters ahead of
+ * it) does not register a PPU waiter and sleep on the queue's lv2 event queue; it releases the line and tries again.
+ * That event queue only exists after cellSpursLFQueueAttachLv2EventQueue, which this runtime answers without
+ * creating one, so the libsre path had nothing to wait on either. A PPU producer therefore never writes 0xFFFF into
+ * the push-waiter ids; if an SPU writes a waiting PPU's 0xFFFF anyway, the wake-up is logged and dropped.
+ *
+ * PS3_LFQ_TRACE=1 (default off) logs every push. */
+#include "cellSpurs.h"
+#include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_context.h"
+#include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_memory.h"
+#include "../../runtime/platform/win32_compat.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+extern PPU_THREAD_LOCAL ppu_context* g_active_ctx;
+extern uint32_t g_ps3_sdk_version;
+void     ppu_resv_snap(uint64_t ea);
+int      ppu_stwcx32(uint64_t ea, uint32_t expected, uint32_t val);
+int      ppu_stdcx64(uint64_t ea, uint64_t expected, uint64_t val);
+void     ps3_hle_register_ctx(uint32_t nid, const char* name, void (*fn)(ppu_context*));
+uint32_t cellSpursHleTasksetByWid(uint32_t spurs_ea, uint32_t wid);
+s32      _cellSpursSendSignal(void* taskset, u32 taskId);
+
+#define LFQ_AGAIN  0x80410101u   /* the libsre-internal codes; the entry points return (code & 0xFF) | 0x80410900 */
+#define LFQ_INVAL  0x80410102u
+#define LFQ_PERM   0x80410109u
+#define LFQ_STAT   0x8041010Fu
+#define LFQ_ALIGN  0x80410110u
+#define LFQ_NULL   0x80410111u
+
+static int lfq_trace(void)
+{
+    static int t = -1;
+    if (t < 0) { const char* e = getenv("PS3_LFQ_TRACE"); t = (e && *e && *e != '0') ? 1 : 0; }
+    return t;
+}
+static uint32_t lfq_ret(uint32_t r) { return (int32_t)r < 0 ? (r & 0xFFu) | 0x80410900u : r; }
+
+/* The guest's lwarx/ldarx and stwcx./stdcx., as the lifter emits them, on the calling thread's context: the same
+ * reservation the libsre code had, so other PPU threads and SPU GETLLAR/PUTLLC see the same atomicity. */
+static uint64_t lfq_ldarx(ppu_context* c, uint32_t ea)
+{
+    ppu_resv_snap(ea);
+    uint64_t v = vm_read64(ea);
+    c->reserve_addr = ea; c->reserve_value = v;
+    return v;
+}
+static int lfq_stdcx(ppu_context* c, uint32_t ea, uint64_t v)
+{
+    int ok = c->reserve_addr == ea && ppu_stdcx64(ea, c->reserve_value, v);
+    c->reserve_addr = 0;
+    return ok;
+}
+static uint32_t lfq_lwarx(ppu_context* c, uint32_t ea)
+{
+    ppu_resv_snap(ea);
+    uint32_t v = vm_read32(ea);
+    c->reserve_addr = ea; c->reserve_value = v;
+    return v;
+}
+static int lfq_stwcx(ppu_context* c, uint32_t ea, uint32_t v)
+{
+    int ok = c->reserve_addr == ea && ppu_stwcx32(ea, (uint32_t)c->reserve_value, v);
+    c->reserve_addr = 0;
+    return ok;
+}
+
+static uint32_t mod30(int32_t d) { return (uint32_t)(d < 0 ? d + 30 : d); }
+/* (x - y) mod 2*depth, the way libsre compares: x may come from a signed halfword (extsh). */
+static int32_t ring_diff(int32_t x, int32_t y, int32_t depth) { return x < y ? x - y + 2 * depth : x - y; }
+static uint16_t f16(uint64_t w, int i) { return (uint16_t)(w >> (48 - 16 * i)); }   /* halfword i of a u64 */
+static uint64_t set16(uint64_t w, int i, uint32_t v)
+{
+    const int sh = 48 - 16 * i;
+    return (w & ~(0xFFFFull << sh)) | ((uint64_t)(v & 0xFFFFu) << sh);
+}
+
+/* ---- _cellSpursLFQueueInitialize ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+
+/* libsre 0x02001F6C: the line for a fresh queue. */
+static void lfq_write_line(uint32_t q, uint32_t buf, uint32_t size, uint32_t depth, uint32_t dir, uint32_t owner)
+{
+    static const unsigned zero16[] = { 0x00, 0x02, 0x06, 0x08, 0x0A, 0x0E };
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof zero16 / sizeof zero16[0]; i++) vm_write16(q + zero16[i], 0);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x10, size);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x14, depth);
+    vm_write64(q + 0x18, buf);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x24, dir);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 16; i++) { vm_write16(q + 0x30 + 2 * i, 0); vm_write16(q + 0x50 + 2 * i, 0); }
+    vm_write64(q + 0x70, owner);
+    if (dir != 3) {
+        vm_write32(q + 0x28, 0);
+        vm_write64(q + 0x78, 0);
+        vm_write32(q + 0x20, 0xFFFFFFFFu);
+        return;
+    }
+    vm_write64(q + 0x18, (uint64_t)buf | 1);
+    vm_write16(q + 0x04, 0);
+    vm_write8(q + 0x20, 0xFF);
+    vm_write8(q + 0x21, 0xFF);
+    vm_write16(q + 0x0C, 0);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x28, 0xFFFFFFFFu);
+    vm_write16(q + 0x30, 0xFFFF);
+    vm_write16(q + 0x50, 0xFFFF);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x78, 0);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x7C, 0);
+}
+
+/* libsre 0x0200209C: argument checks, then the init state at +0x2C (0 -> 1 -> 2) so one caller builds the line. */
+static uint32_t lfq_init(ppu_context* c, uint32_t q, uint32_t buf, uint32_t size, uint32_t depth, uint32_t dir,
+                         uint32_t owner)
+{
+    if (!q) return LFQ_NULL;
+    if (size) {
+        if (!buf) return LFQ_NULL;
+        if (size > 0x4000 || (size & 0xF)) return LFQ_INVAL;
+    }
+    if (!depth || (depth & 0xFFFF8000u) || dir > 3) return LFQ_INVAL;
+    if ((q & 0x7F) || (buf & 0xF)) return LFQ_ALIGN;
+
+    /* sys_process_get_sdk_version, as libsre asks it (the syscall handler's own override included). */
+    const char* ov = getenv("PS3_SDK_VERSION");
+    uint32_t sdk = ov && *ov ? (uint32_t)strtoul(ov, NULL, 0) : g_ps3_sdk_version;
+    if (sdk == 0xFFFFFFFFu) sdk = 0x00493000;
+    const int checked = sdk > 0x0017FFFF;
+
+    uint32_t state;
+    for (;;) {
+        state = lfq_lwarx(c, q + 0x2C);
+        uint32_t next = state;
+        if (state == 0) {
+            if (checked)
+                for (unsigned i = 0; i < 16; i++)
+                    if (vm_read64(q + 8 * i)) { c->reserve_addr = 0; return LFQ_STAT; }
+            next = 1;
+        } else if (checked && state != 2) {
+            c->reserve_addr = 0;
+            return LFQ_STAT;
+        }
+        if (lfq_stwcx(c, q + 0x2C, next)) { state = next; break; }
+    }
+    if (state == 2) {   /* already built: the arguments must be the ones it was built with */
+        if (vm_read32(q + 0x10) != size || vm_read32(q + 0x14) != depth || vm_read64(q + 0x18) != buf)
+            return LFQ_INVAL;
+        if (checked && (vm_read64(q + 0x70) != owner || vm_read32(q + 0x24) != dir)) return LFQ_INVAL;
+        return 0;
+    }
+    lfq_write_line(q, buf, size, depth, dir, owner);
+    vm_write32(q + 0x2C, 2);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+uint32_t cellSpursLFQueueHleInitialize(ppu_context* c, uint32_t owner, uint32_t q, uint32_t buf, uint32_t size,
+                                       uint32_t depth, uint32_t dir)
+{
+    /* libsre 0x02017134: an aligned owner is a taskset, and one past the queue limit is refused. */
+    if (!(owner & 0xF) && vm_read32(owner + 0x74) > 31) return 0x80410902u;
+    return lfq_ret(lfq_init(c, q, buf, size, depth, dir, owner));
+}
+
+/* ---- _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* The wake-up the push hands to fpSendSignal (libsre's own cellSpursSendSignal). A queue owned by a SPURS instance
+ * rather than a taskset signals (spurs | 1, wid << 8 | task); libsre resolves the wid through workload data this HLE
+ * does not keep, so the HLE's taskset table answers. Settable for tests. */
+static int32_t lfq_send_signal(uint32_t ea, uint32_t id)
+{
+    if ((ea & 0xF) == 1) {
+        const uint32_t spurs = ea & ~0xFu, wid = id >> 8;
+        ea = cellSpursHleTasksetByWid(spurs, wid);
+        if (!ea) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] no taskset for spurs 0x%08X wid %u (task %u)\n", spurs, wid, id & 0xFF);
+            return (int32_t)0x80410905;   /* CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_SRCH */
+        }
+        id &= 0xFF;
+    }
+    return _cellSpursSendSignal((void*)(uintptr_t)ea, id);
+}
+int32_t (*cellSpursLFQueueHleSignal)(uint32_t ea, uint32_t id) = lfq_send_signal;
+
+/* libsre 0x020030B8 (ANY2ANY, with useEventQueue = 1 as the push passes it): reserve the next push index. Returns 0
+ * and the index, LFQ_AGAIN when the queue cannot take the push now and the caller may not wait, or 1 when libsre would
+ * register this thread as a waiter (see the top of the file: the caller tries again instead). */
+static uint32_t lfq_reserve(ppu_context* c, uint32_t q, uint32_t is_blocking, int32_t* pos)
+{
+    const int32_t depth = (int32_t)vm_read32(q + 0x14);
+    for (;;) {
+        uint64_t P = lfq_ldarx(c, q + 8);
+        const uint64_t Q = vm_read64(q);
+        const int32_t r4 = (int16_t)f16(P, 3);
+        const int32_t occ = ring_diff(r4, f16(Q, 0), depth);         /* reserved pushes not yet popped */
+        const int32_t inflight = ring_diff(r4, f16(P, 0), depth);    /* reserved pushes not yet committed */
+        const uint32_t pk = f16(P, 2), pc = pk & 31, pb = (pk >> 5) & 31, pa = (pk >> 10) & 31;
+        const uint32_t waiting = mod30((int32_t)pc - (int32_t)pa), woken = mod30((int32_t)pa - (int32_t)pb);
+        int blocked = occ + (int32_t)woken >= depth || inflight + (int32_t)woken > 15 || waiting != 0;
+        const int ring_full = waiting == 15 || woken == 15;
+        *pos = r4;
+        if (!blocked) {
+            const int32_t next = r4 + 1 < 2 * depth ? r4 + 1 : 0;
+            if (lfq_stdcx(c, q + 8, set16(P, 3, (uint32_t)next))) return 0;
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (ring_full || !is_blocking) {   /* libsre commits the line unchanged, then answers AGAIN */
+            if (lfq_stdcx(c, q + 8, P)) return LFQ_AGAIN;
+            continue;
+        }
+        c->reserve_addr = 0;
+        return 1;
+    }
+}
+
+/* libsre 0x0200439C: hand out the wake-ups the commit collected. */
+static uint32_t lfq_dispatch(uint32_t q, const uint32_t* ids, uint32_t n)
+{
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        const uint32_t id = ids[i];
+        if ((id & 0xFF00) == 0xFF00) {   /* a waiting PPU thread: libsre sends to its event port */
+            const uint32_t port = (id & 0xFF) == 1 ? vm_read32(q + 0x28)
+                                                   : ((uint32_t)vm_read16(q + 0x30) << 16) | vm_read16(q + 0x50);
+            if (port == 0xFFFFFFFFu) return LFQ_PERM;
+            static int warned;
+            if (!warned++) fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] q=0x%08X: a PPU waiter's event port 0x%08X, not sent\n", q, port);
+            continue;
+        }
+        const int32_t r = cellSpursLFQueueHleSignal(vm_read32(q + 0x74), id);
+        if (r) return (uint32_t)r;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* libsre 0x020035C8 (ANY2ANY): commit the push at `pos` and wake the waiters the commit lets through, one per element
+ * that becomes visible: the pop waiters (SPU consumers waiting for data) first, then the push waiters. A wake-up
+ * moves the pop-waiter pack in Q, so then Q is committed first and P after it, with P unchanged since it was read. */
+static uint32_t lfq_complete(ppu_context* c, uint32_t q, int32_t pos)
+{
+    const int32_t depth = (int32_t)vm_read32(q + 0x14);
+    uint32_t ids[64], total = 0;
+    int mode_q = 0;   /* libsre's second form: the reservation on Q */
+    for (;;) {
+        uint64_t P, Q;
+        if (!mode_q) { P = lfq_ldarx(c, q + 8); Q = vm_read64(q); }
+        else         { Q = lfq_ldarx(c, q);     P = vm_read64(q + 8); }
+        const uint64_t P_read = P;
+        const int32_t P0 = f16(P, 0), Q0 = f16(Q, 0);
+        const int32_t off = ring_diff(pos, P0, depth);
+        uint32_t qpk = f16(Q, 2), ppk = f16(P, 2);
+        const uint32_t qa = (qpk >> 10) & 31, qb = (qpk >> 5) & 31, pa = (ppk >> 10) & 31, pb = (ppk >> 5) & 31;
+        int32_t q_busy = ring_diff((int16_t)f16(Q, 3), Q0, depth) + (int32_t)mod30((int32_t)qa - (int32_t)qb);
+        int32_t p_busy = ring_diff((int16_t)f16(P, 3), Q0, depth) + (int32_t)mod30((int32_t)pa - (int32_t)pb);
+        const uint32_t sh = (uint32_t)(15 - off) & 63;
+        uint32_t mask = f16(P, 1) | (sh < 32 ? 1u << sh : 0);
+        uint32_t run = 0;
+        while (run < 16 && (mask & (0x8000u >> run))) run++;
+        int32_t p0 = P0 + (int32_t)run;
+        if (p0 >= 2 * depth) p0 -= 2 * depth;
+        int32_t q_wait = q_busy <= 15 ? (int32_t)mod30((int32_t)(qpk & 31) - (int32_t)qa) : 0;
+        int32_t p_wait = depth > p_busy ? (int32_t)mod30((int32_t)(ppk & 31) - (int32_t)pa) : 0;
+        P = set16(set16(P, 0, (uint32_t)p0), 1, (mask << run) & 0xFFFF);
+        uint32_t n = 0;
+        int restart = 0;
+        for (int32_t k = (int32_t)run - 1; k >= 0 && !restart; k--) {
+            if (!((int32_t)total > k) && q_wait && q_busy <= 15) {
+                const uint32_t a = (qpk >> 10) & 31;
+                const uint32_t id = vm_read16(q + 0x32 + 2 * (a > 14 ? a - 15 : a));
+                if (total + n < 64) ids[total + n] = id == 0xFFFF ? 0xFF01 : id;
+                if (!mode_q) { mode_q = 1; restart = 1; break; }
+                qpk = (qpk & ~(31u << 10)) | (a == 29 ? 0 : (a + 1) << 10);
+                n++; q_busy++; q_wait--;
+            }
+            if (p_wait && p_busy < depth) {
+                const uint32_t a = (ppk >> 10) & 31;
+                const uint32_t id = vm_read16(q + 0x52 + 2 * (a > 14 ? a - 15 : a));
+                if (total + n < 64) ids[total + n] = id == 0xFFFF ? 0xFF02 : id;
+                ppk = (ppk & ~(31u << 10)) | (a == 29 ? 0 : (a + 1) << 10);
+                n++; p_busy++; p_wait--;
+            }
+        }
+        if (restart) { c->reserve_addr = 0; continue; }
+        P = set16(P, 2, ppk);
+        if (!mode_q) {
+            if (!lfq_stdcx(c, q + 8, P)) continue;
+            total += n;
+            break;
+        }
+        /* libsre retries a failed Q commit through its P load (one reservation granule on the Cell); here the retry
+         * reserves Q again, which is what that granule gave it. */
+        if (!lfq_stdcx(c, q, set16(Q, 2, qpk))) continue;
+        total += n;
+        int again = 0;
+        for (;;) {
+            const uint64_t now = lfq_ldarx(c, q + 8);
+            if (now != P_read || vm_read16(q + 4) != qpk) { c->reserve_addr = 0; again = 1; break; }
+            if (lfq_stdcx(c, q + 8, P)) break;
+        }
+        if (!again) break;
+    }
+    if (total > 64) { fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] q=0x%08X: %u wake-ups, 64 sent\n", q, total); total = 64; }
+    return lfq_dispatch(q, ids, total);
+}
+
+uint32_t cellSpursLFQueueHlePushBody(ppu_context* c, uint32_t q, uint32_t data, uint32_t is_blocking)
+{
+    if (q & 0x7F) return 0x80410910u;
+    if (!q || !data) return 0x80410911u;
+    const uint32_t dir = vm_read32(q + 0x24);
+    if (dir != 3) {
+        /* libsre's PPU2SPU push (0x020024F4) is not written here; the direction checks it starts with are. */
+        if (dir == 2) {
+            static int warned;
+            if (!warned++) fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] q=0x%08X: a direction-2 push is not implemented\n", q);
+        }
+        return lfq_ret(LFQ_PERM);
+    }
+    int32_t pos;
+    uint32_t r;
+    for (unsigned spins = 0; (r = lfq_reserve(c, q, is_blocking, &pos)) == 1; spins++) {
+        if (lfq_trace() && (spins == 1000 || spins % 30000 == 29999))
+            fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] push q=0x%08X waiting for room, %u tries\n", q, spins);
+        Sleep(spins < 64 ? 0 : 1);
+    }
+    if (r) return lfq_ret(r);
+    const int32_t depth = (int32_t)vm_read32(q + 0x14);
+    const uint32_t size = vm_read32(q + 0x10);
+    const uint32_t slot = (uint32_t)(pos >= depth ? pos - depth : pos);
+    const uint32_t dst = ((uint32_t)vm_read64(q + 0x18) & ~1u) + size * slot;
+    for (uint32_t o = 0; o < size;) {   /* coherent, a 128-byte line at a time */
+        const uint32_t n = 128 - ((dst + o) & 127) < size - o ? 128 - ((dst + o) & 127) : size - o;
+        VM_WRITE_COH(dst + o, vm_ptr8(data + o), n);
+        o += n;
+    }
+    r = lfq_complete(c, q, pos);
+    if (lfq_trace())
+        fprintf(stderr, "[lfq] push q=0x%08X pos=%d slot=0x%08X -> 0x%08X line %016llX %016llX\n", q, pos, dst, r,
+                (unsigned long long)vm_read64(q), (unsigned long long)vm_read64(q + 8));
+    if (r == 0x80410902u || r == 0x8041090Fu) return 0x80410914u;
+    return lfq_ret(r);
+}
+
+/* ---- the imports ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+
+/* Both take the calling thread's context: their store-conditionals need its reservation. */
+static void hle_lfq_init(ppu_context* ctx)
+{
+    ppu_context* const active = g_active_ctx;
+    g_active_ctx = ctx;
+    ctx->gpr[3] = (uint64_t)(int64_t)(int32_t)cellSpursLFQueueHleInitialize(
+        ctx, (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[3], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[4], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[5], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[6],
+        (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[7], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[8]);
+    g_active_ctx = active;
+}
+static void hle_lfq_push(ppu_context* ctx)
+{
+    ppu_context* const active = g_active_ctx;
+    g_active_ctx = ctx;
+    ctx->gpr[3] = (uint64_t)(int64_t)(int32_t)cellSpursLFQueueHlePushBody(
+        ctx, (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[3], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[4], (uint32_t)ctx->gpr[5]);
+    g_active_ctx = active;
+}
+
+void cellSpursLFQueue_register_ctx_handlers(void)
+{
+    ps3_hle_register_ctx(0x011EE38Bu, "_cellSpursLFQueueInitialize", hle_lfq_init);
+    ps3_hle_register_ctx(0x8A85674Du, "_cellSpursLFQueuePushBody", hle_lfq_push);
+}
